---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Operational Efficiency"
  description="Process automation, CRM setup, internal tooling, and workflows for service businesses in Golden, CO and the Front Range. ZeisWorks builds and fixes the systems most owners can't see."
  ogTitle="Operational Efficiency | zeisWorks"
  ogDescription="The systems that make growth stick. CRM setup, process automation, and workflows for Golden and Front Range businesses."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 space-y-16">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-orange uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">02 / Operations</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold text-ink leading-tight">
        Operational efficiency
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-mid text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
        Your business runs on systems most owners can't see. I build, fix, and automate them. CRM systems, custom workflows, and the integrations that connect everything you already use.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-modal="gap-analysis"
          class="bg-navy text-cream text-sm px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-navy/90 transition-colors font-medium inline-block cursor-pointer border-0"
        >
          Get in touch →
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What's included -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6">What's included</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4">
        {[
          { title: 'CRM setup and cleanup', body: 'Salesforce and HubSpot builds from scratch or overhauls of existing installs. Data cleanup, field mapping, pipeline design, and user training.' },
          { title: 'Process automation', body: 'Identifying the manual processes that drain time and building the automations that replace them. From simple Zapier workflows to complex n8n pipelines.' },
          { title: 'Workflow design', body: 'Mapping how work actually moves through your business, finding the gaps, and designing the systems to close them.' },
          { title: 'Reporting and dashboards', body: 'Reports that answer real business questions, not just data exports. Built in your CRM, in a BI tool, or as a custom-built dashboard.' },
          { title: 'Systems integration', body: 'Connecting the tools your team already uses so data stops living in silos. CRM to accounting, marketing to sales, quoting to invoicing.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
            <span class="mt-1.5 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-orange shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-ink font-medium">{item.title}.</strong>{' '}
              <span class="text-ink-mid">{item.body}</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Who it's for -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4">Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-mid leading-relaxed mb-4">
        This pillar fits businesses that have outgrown spreadsheets but haven't been able to get their CRM or workflows to actually work. Common situations:
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        {[
          'CRM that nobody updates because it\'s faster to use a spreadsheet',
          'Manual processes three people do because nobody\'s built the automation',
          'Software you\'re paying for that half the team doesn\'t use',
          'Reports that take 2 hours to pull and are still probably wrong',
          'Data scattered across tools with no clean source of truth',
          'New CRM needed but nobody has time to scope and build it',
        ].map(situation => (
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-cream-dark bg-cream p-4 text-sm text-ink-mid">{situation}</div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Outcomes -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4">What outcomes look like</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-ink-mid leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          A professional services firm with 12 people and a Salesforce install nobody trusts. Two years of data, but half the records are incomplete, the pipeline is cluttered with closed deals nobody archived, and the weekly sales report takes the ops manager 90 minutes to assemble. A six-week cleanup and rebuild changes all of that. The data gets clean, the pipeline makes sense, and the report runs in two clicks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Operational efficiency work has the highest retention rate of anything ZeisWorks does. Clients who run their operations through these systems don't leave easily, because the systems are working and the cost of switching is real. That's a sign the work was done right.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy/20 bg-navy/5 p-8">
      <p class="text-xs text-navy uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Next step</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Describe the problem. Get a free plan.</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-mid mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        You don't need to know what the solution is. Describing what's broken or slow is enough. I'll come back with a specific plan: what I'd do, how long it takes, what it costs. Free, no commitment.
      </p>
      <button
        type="button"
        data-modal="gap-analysis"
        class="inline-block bg-navy text-cream text-sm px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-medium hover:bg-navy/90 transition-colors cursor-pointer border-0"
      >
        Get in touch
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Back -->
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-light">
      <a href="/marketing" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">← Marketing</a>
      &nbsp;·&nbsp;
      <a href="/custom-tools" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">Custom Tools →</a>
    </p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
